  "source": "NEET 2025",
  "question": "To an ac power supply of $220$ V at $50$ Hz, a resistor of $20\\ \\Omega$, a capacitor of reactance $25\\ \\Omega$ and an inductor of reactance $45\\ \\Omega$ are connected in series. The corresponding current in the circuit and the phase angle between the current and the voltage is, respectively -",
  "diagram": "",
  "diagram_alt": "",
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "$7.8$ A and $30°$",
      "image": ""
    },
    {
      "text": "$7.8$ A and $45°$",
      "image": ""
    },
    {
      "text": "$15.6$ A and $30°$",
      "image": ""
    },
    {
      "text": "$15.6$ A and $45°$",
      "image": ""
    }
  ],
  "answer": "B",
  "numerical_answer": "",
  "tolerance": "",
  "solution": "$$Z = \\sqrt{R^2 + (X_L - X_C)^2} = \\sqrt{20^2 + (45 - 25)^2} = 20\\sqrt{2} \\approx 28.3\\ \\Omega$$\n\n$$I = \\frac{220}{28.3} \\approx 7.8\\ \\text{A}$$\n\n$$\\tan\\phi = \\frac{X_L - X_C}{R} = \\frac{20}{20} = 1 \\;\\Rightarrow\\; \\phi = 45°$$",
